1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,019
The worst way to find out an automation broke? Your client tells you.

2
00:00:04,469 --> 00:00:08,480
So every client workflow I build gets one setting: an error workflow.

3
00:00:08,930 --> 00:00:17,165
Here's a real run. An enquiry comes in, gets cleaned up, and then the Google Sheets step fails. The connection has no access token.

4
00:00:17,615 --> 00:00:22,777
n8n hands the failure straight to the error workflow. It builds an alert and emails it.

5
00:00:23,227 --> 00:00:28,625
The email names the workflow, the step that failed, the exact error, and links to the execution.

6
00:00:29,075 --> 00:00:36,989
Pick the same alert workflow in each of your client's workflows. One tip: it only fires on live runs, not when you test in the editor.

7
00:00:37,439 --> 00:00:42,538
Follow for the next real n8n build, or DM FLOW for the free enquiry workflow.

